<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 was closed on 5 October, but one of its problems is still open. The parser fix and the
retired form do not touch the <code>one-day</code> reports.
</Callout>

## The three problems

- **`parser`** · fixed (`fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales`). The shared parser read every
  date month first, and every tenant on file writes the day first. 7 April went out as 4 July.
- **`hint`** · won't fix: the `booking-v3` form is retired. It printed `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date
  field, people typed what it said, and the form read the date day first. Only through that form,
  at three tenants.
- **`one-day`** · open. The date moves by one day, not by a swap: Tuesday in Lisbon, Monday in
  Toronto. It points to a time-zone conversion. The desk noted these reports and filed them under
  the parser by tenant, so closing #4471 closed them too, without a fix.

## Why they were merged

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) merges reports on subject line alone. All
three problems come in under the same subjects ("Wrong day on the invite", "Date is wrong"), so
the subject rule put them in one ticket. Intake's tag did not help: it is a guess from the
reporter's browser, and the desk's cause comes from the tenant.

What the desk saw, as the #4471 page shows it:

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

## For the desk

- Close a merged ticket per problem, not per ticket: check each problem's outcome before the
  reports it covers go quiet.
- Count reports by cause, not by subject (`sameCause`, try it on the [triage page](/kb/triage/dedupe)),
  and read the body: a one-day move gets the parser's cause from its tenant, but it is not a swap.
- Decision 0001 is accepted, so it stays as written. Replacing it needs a new record.
- The export repeats some reports across its pages. Count unique ids, as the tables here do.

